steps.text:
Yes—this is supported publicly in MUI v5:

```ts
import { styled, useThemeProps } from '@mui/material/styles';

const MyCustomComponentRoot = styled('div', {
  name: 'MuiMyCustomComponent',
  slot: 'Root',
})(({ theme }) => ({
  padding: theme.spacing(1),
}));

export function MyCustomComponent(inProps) {
  const props = useThemeProps({
    props: inProps,
    name: 'MuiMyCustomComponent',
  });

  return <MyCustomComponentRoot {...props} />;
}
```

`useThemeProps` applies `theme.components.MuiMyCustomComponent.defaultProps`. The `styled()` configuration—particularly `name` and the root slot—also enables `styleOverrides` and `variants` from the theme.

```ts
const theme = createTheme({
  components: {
    MuiMyCustomComponent: {
      variants: [
        {
          props: { variant: 'dashed' },
          style: { border: '2px dashed blue' },
        },
      ],
    },
  },
});
```

For TypeScript, module-augment `@mui/material/styles` to register the custom component’s props, slots, overrides, and variants; otherwise `components.MuiMyCustomComponent` will not be type-safe.
